WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.190
- Hey, what's up, I'm Brenda.

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:02.850
I'm a Tasty producer and today

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.141
we're gonna be making my
favorite Hispanic recipes.

00:00:06.141 --> 00:00:08.371
(funky upbeat music)

00:00:08.371 --> 00:00:12.770
Tortilla espanola is a dish
that originates in Spain.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.810
They will eat it in gatherings,
mostly during the summer.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.770
They can eat it cold and hot.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.630
And the reason why I created this,

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.590
it's because my dad's
family have Spain heritage.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.160
So realizing that this
is a very popular dish,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.360
I wanna explore that
other half of my culture

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.170
that I haven't been
really connecting with.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.490
So, when I made this,
it's not only very simple

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.410
but it's very delicious even
though a lot of people here

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.713
were not exposed to it.

00:00:35.713 --> 00:00:37.870
They're familiar with this dish

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.790
but the ingredients are so common

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.460
that people of all kinds enjoyed it

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.560
and ask me for the recipe
because that's how good it was.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.760
And I thought well, this
is the perfect excuse

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.760
to learn something new and to explore.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.990
And when I made it, I realized that it has

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:56.640
a lot of commonalities with
the South American culture.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.520
Not only that but this simple dish

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.190
has a lot of potential
to connect with people

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.610
who are not even Latin American

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.160
because the ingredients are so common.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.440
So, really, you have
don't have to go to Spain

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.150
to get a little authentic
taste of this culture.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.290
You can just grab a
couple of tomatoes, eggs,

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:14.220
and then play with this ingredients

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.123
and you will be eating
authentic Spaniard cuisine.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:23.100
One of my favorite
recipes called aborrajados

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.810
because it's Columbian
which is where I'm from.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.830
Also because it's super
easy and delicious.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.560
So, this is the first video that I make

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.350
which is amazing, it's great.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.820
But get this, I'm making
this with Adam Bianchi

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.880
which you probably know from Worth It.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.210
So, there comes a part where
we have to get the aborrajados

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.130
and break it in half and get
that beautiful cheese pull

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.020
and this dude looks at me,
the pressure takes over,

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.530
and there I am breaking that thing

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.580
as he's looking at me like you can do it!

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.890
And it happened.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.253
It was incredible.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.090
I managed to get a smile out of Bianchi.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.130
You know he never smiles while I did

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.750
and I'm still in the books, on record,

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.313
as the one and only
person who made him smile.

00:02:05.276 --> 00:02:06.109
(bell chiming)

00:02:06.109 --> 00:02:07.840
When we published it, in the comments,

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.760
a lot of people were starting claiming

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.903
this recipe as theirs.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.880
Meaning, Ecuadorian people were saying

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.803
that's actually Ecuadorian,
Peruvians, Puerto Ricans.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.514
So, it was really cool to realize

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:23.370
okay, this is what I thought
was a Columbian recipe,

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.660
it's actually this Latin American recipe

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.860
that a lot of people are
calling different names

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.430
and making it in different
ways so it's ours.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.940
It was kind of enlightening to realize

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.240
that what I thought was ours
is really Latin American.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.440
And it's so easy.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:41.290
Really all you're doing is
grabbing some sweet plantains,

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.300
frying it, flattening it,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.100
and then you put whatever you want inside.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.200
In Columbia, we put a little bit of cheese

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.470
and sometimes a little bit of guava paste.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:52.620
It's so amazing to see those
different interpretations

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.023
of such a delicious, simple dish.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:55.953
And guess what?

00:02:55.953 --> 00:02:57.580
Not only did we get the cheese pull,

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.570
it was one of the most successful videos

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.973
that we had on Bien
Tasty so thank you Adam.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.750
Alright, you and I know that bread pudding

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.410
does not belong to
Columbia or Latin America

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.930
but it's a very popular dessert.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:13.880
Because what you're really
doing is grabbing any extra

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.880
bread that you have laying around home

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.290
and adding whatever you want.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.820
In this case, I noticed that
there was a little twist.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.300
People were adding a little
bit of dulce de leche

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.003
which is flat caramel.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:29.295
And instead of just sugar and heavy cream,

00:03:29.295 --> 00:03:33.220
we were adding condensed
milk which has everything.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.750
It's creamy, it has the sugar, it's milky

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:38.193
so you have everything
in this one ingredient.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.070
When this was ready to
go out, people tried it.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.140
There was this girl at
work, her name is Merrill.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.790
She never had it before,
not in this way at least,

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.690
and she said, can I
just grab a little bit?

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.390
Can I grab a little bit more?

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.220
It was so popular and a lot of people

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:55.030
were texting me for recipes and begging me

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:58.030
to please make it all
over again and so I did.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.953
If you wanna please a big
crowd, this is your option.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.620
So, green plantain gives
us a couple of things.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.220
We char tostones also known as patacones

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.510
in my country in Columbia.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.860
So, tostones is really just green plantain

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.010
that has been fried
and then it's flattened

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.290
and then it's fried again.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.400
So, as I'm going through
Instagram, I realize

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.750
that there a couple of places in Columbia

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.650
who are making this plantain cone

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.630
and it's super cool because now you have

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.913
amazing, delicious plantain
with a filling on the go.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.253
Inspired by all of this
post and this new trend,

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.260
I decided to bring it to Tasty.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:34.210
And to my surprise, it
was super successful.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.220
A lot of people from different cultures

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.960
embraced this idea and soon after,

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.550
articles from around the world

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:43.120
started talking about this plantain cone,

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.750
which again, not my creation

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.350
but it was trending in my country.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.210
And now, the whole
continent knew about it.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.126
It was cool to realize that
by publishing this video,

00:04:52.126 --> 00:04:55.110
I was somehow highlighting
this little dish

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.600
in a little tiny corner of a country

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.940
and at the end of the day,
a lot of small business

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.850
benefited because their
recipe becomes popular

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.850
and it's super cool because now you have

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:07.950
amazing, delicious plantain
with a filling on the go

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.173
inspired by all this
post and this new trend.

00:05:11.362 --> 00:05:13.852
(soft electronic music)

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.750
Papas rellenas is very popular in places

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.480
like Peru and Columbia.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.590
All it really is is mashed potato

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.310
which houses whatever you want.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.583
It can be beans, ground beef,

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.410
and that's really the whole concept.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:30.440
So, I came to the United States
when I was about to turn 15

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.680
and one of the things
that I noticed immediately

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:36.450
is that although people do
try to bring back the dishes

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:40.113
from different countries, there
was something missing here.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.898
Now that I'm working at Bien Tasty,

00:05:41.898 --> 00:05:45.280
I get to share those dishes that I miss

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.853
so much when I arrived.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.868
And I get to share them
with a lot of people

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.743
in a lot of countries.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.630
So, it's crazy how
things played out for me

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.910
to be able to still work with my culture

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.068
as part of my job.

00:05:58.068 --> 00:05:59.253
That's insane.

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:02.983
Every single dish, it's an
expression of some kind.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.976
Maybe it's a really fancy chef

00:06:04.976 --> 00:06:09.220
who wants to show off his
amazing culinary skills

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.566
or it's just a grandma in Ecuador

00:06:11.566 --> 00:06:16.018
who is really eager to
share her longtime tradition

00:06:16.018 --> 00:06:18.610
of papas rellenas, whatever it is.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.640
It's a message in every dish.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.510
At the end of the day, you're eating

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:24.283
a little bit of someone's story.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.230
Maybe it's just a story of how this

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:28.230
dish arrived to existence.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.300
Maybe it's a story of the influence

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.640
of other cultures to yours.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:36.348
Whatever it is, as a fan of
stories, of storytelling,

00:06:36.348 --> 00:06:39.100
I try to appreciate as much as I can

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.303
and a new dish, not just for
its flavors and its looks,

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:43.763
but for its origins.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.460
And that's something that
I'm lucky enough to do

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.790
in every single video
that I'm putting out there

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:51.080
for Bien Tasty and I get to do it with

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.453
a massive audience.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:54.130
Alright, so if you haven't gotten a chance

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:57.640
to explore non-mainstream
Latin American recipes

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.840
then please, I beg you to try these ones,

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:01.750
because they are delicious,
they're easy to make,

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.660
they're affordable, and most importantly,

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:08.563
you will be eating authentic,
amazing Latin American dishes.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:09.423
Try them.

00:07:09.547 --> 00:07:13.047
(upbeat electronic music)

